# Boss lines that know about the army (Common/Compat/Calamity/BossLines.cs).
# Each key is the last part of a Calamity key "Mods.CalamityMod.Status.Boss.<key>". While 3 or more levies are deployed and "Boss lines acknowledge your army" is on,
# the boss says the line below in place of its own. A line that already fits an army has no entry here and is said as Calamity wrote it.
# Keep each line's point and tone; change only what assumes the player fights alone.

# shown after the army version when "Show the original boss line too" is on
OriginalLine: (original) {0}
# ---- Supreme Witch Calamitas, the first battle
SCalSummonText: Do you enjoy dragging all of them through hell?
SCalStartText: You should have just died... all of you.
SCalBH2Text: It wasn't too long ago you and your rabble barely managed to defeat my doppelganger. Quite the failure, wasn't it?
SCalBH3Text: You take all this power, and what do you do with it? Build an army?
SCalBrothersText: You brought your family. Would you like to meet mine? Horrible, isn't it?
SCalPhase2Text: You will all suffer greatly.
SCalBH4Text: It's absurd to even think of trying to get away. As long as any of you live, you will suffer.
SCalSeekerRingText: An upstart who stole and killed their way to power, then armed a following with it. I wonder, who does that remind me of...?
SCalBH5Text: None of you have any stake in this battle. No one gave you any say in this matter!
SCalSepulcher2Text: Once the dust has settled and only your army remains, what value will this have had?!
SCalAcceptanceText2: I have no more energy left to resent him, or you, or any of them...
SCalAcceptanceText3: It will all be in your hands now. Yours, and theirs.
# ---- Supreme Witch Calamitas, the rematch
SCalSummonTextRematch: Hm? You want me to fight all of you? So be it.
SCalStartTextRematch: When the time comes, would you all wish to be part of my creation?
SCalBH2TextRematch: Don't expect this to be easy. I have destroyed armies like these many times.
SCalBH3TextRematch: I haven't had such interesting target dummies to test my magic on in a long time.
SCalBH4TextRematch: Most soldiers were terrified of fighting me. I wonder if they are too?
SCalSeekerRingTextRematch: Their skill is incredible. You have fostered something truly immense.
SCalDesparationText1Rematch: An incredible display of discipline. I concede this match.
SCalDesparationText2Rematch: With their strength alone, you would no doubt face a greater threat than I.
SCalDesparationText4Rematch: I cannot imagine what comes next for someone of your caliber.
# ---- Draedon: the introduction
DraedonIntroductionText2: Your nature fascinates me. You gain all this power, and you give it away. I do not understand it.
DraedonIntroductionText3: You and your soldiers will face my creations, which have surpassed gods.
DraedonIntroductionText4: And you will show me your disposition, and theirs, through battle.
# ---- Draedon: during the Exo Mechs
DraedonExoPhase2Text1: Your army's performance falls neatly within the margins of error.
DraedonExoPhase3Text1: Ever since I was alerted to your presence, I have processed your battles, and your army's, in order to make my machines stronger.
DraedonExoPhase3Text2: Even now, I monitor every one of you. Nothing should escape the bounds of my calculations.
DraedonExoPhase4Text2: You and your soldiers progress steadily against more difficult challenges.
DraedonExoPhase5Text1: Your nature remains unknown to me. They follow you with a loyalty I have seen once before, and even he did not give away this much.
# ---- Draedon: after the battle
DraedonEndText1: An unknown factor--a catalyst is what you are. And you have made catalysts of all of them.
DraedonEndText5: You and yours have also spilled blood, but it may be enough to usher a new age... Of what, I do not know. But it is something I am eager to see.
